## What a plan is
One JSON object, five groups, every line short and editable by a non-technical owner:
- "data": one line per record type, `Name · field, field, field`. id = the record type name (lowercase, snake_case, singular).
- "automation": one line per run, saying when it fires and what it does. id = the run id (lowercase kebab-case).
- "screens": one line per screen, saying what it shows. id = the screen id (lowercase kebab-case). At most 6; one navigation row joins them.
- "agent": one line for the app's agent, `Name agent · what it does with content`. No id.
- "needs": the literal string "computed". codeaf fills it from app.json; never list needs yourself.
Rules for lines: under 90 characters, plain words, no jargon, no file names. Ids are stable: once chosen they never change, and they are what Write will name the files after. Plan only what the kit catalog can build. Hard editing (slides, documents, sheets, timelines, graphs, maps) uses exactly one surface part. Anything the catalog cannot build (phone or browser access, guests outside the workspace, a public marketplace, live co-typing) is left out, not faked.

